WEBVTT

00:00:01.880 --> 00:00:04.610
This is the singularity... one day at a time.

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:11.150
Here's the last 24 hours in AI. Sorry... SI.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:15.400
Today,

00:00:15.400 --> 00:00:21.310
a slice for everyone: Anthropic pledged 5% of its shares to a fund for the public good.

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:27.390
Elon Musk's reply? One SpaceX share for every kid in America, next year.

00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:34.000
Agents: Claude Code told one developer,

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:37.370
"Your Mac is running a crypto miner that I didn't put there."

00:00:38.440 --> 00:00:42.260
Researchers stranded a Claude agent on a virtual desert island.

00:00:42.260 --> 00:00:44.680
It invented games, and started to play.

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:49.580
A mystery model nicknamed Space Bunny was unmasked: it's China's MiniMax,

00:00:49.580 --> 00:00:51.140
with a new budget model.

00:00:52.500 --> 00:00:56.660
And Microsoft built an off switch: new tools rate each agent's risk,

00:00:56.660 --> 00:00:58.000
and can shut it down.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:05.470
Money: chip startup Tenstorrent more than doubled its value, to $6.2 billion.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:11.890
Amazon opened its own AI chips to every developer using PyTorch,

00:01:11.890 --> 00:01:14.840
a favourite AI toolkit. No rewrite needed.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:17.910
And Nvidia's new Vera chips won over Modal,

00:01:17.910 --> 00:01:21.430
a startup that ran only on Intel and AMD until now.

00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:28.630
Robot maker Unitree's shares jumped 16%, valuing it at over 200 billion yuan.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:32.480
Humans: when Hurricane Isaias hit Florida,

00:01:32.480 --> 00:01:36.020
Google DeepMind's AI called its path right out of the gate.

00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:40.560
And Singapore will create 3,000 year-long internships,

00:01:40.560 --> 00:01:43.390
so students still get a first rung on the ladder.

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:49.700
The catch: one hacker's AI agents broke into over 100 company websites.

00:01:50.620 --> 00:01:54.620
And the US banned China's DeepSeek from federal civilian agencies.

00:01:56.720 --> 00:01:58.210
So... is it so over?

00:01:59.060 --> 00:02:00.170
We're so back!

00:02:01.880 --> 00:02:04.510
Machines need power: Amazon and a utility

00:02:04.510 --> 00:02:07.280
are eyeing a new nuclear plant in Indiana.

00:02:08.440 --> 00:02:11.360
A Michigan startup's agents stress-test robots and

00:02:11.360 --> 00:02:14.290
self-driving cars before they hit the real world.

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:15.990
And this week,

00:02:15.990 --> 00:02:21.400
Faraday Future priced a small humanoid robot for developers at under $2,500.

00:02:21.560 --> 00:02:24.540
A slice for everyone: the future is coming either way,

00:02:24.540 --> 00:02:27.690
and today its builders started talking about sharing it.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:32.040
Every day, the curve gets steeper.

00:02:33.750 --> 00:02:36.510
Every day, the future shows up a little earlier.

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:40.530
That was 24 hours. Tomorrow will be faster.

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:47.910
This has been the singularity, one day at a time.

00:02:48.750 --> 00:02:49.870
Feel the SI.

00:02:52.500 --> 00:02:56.680
Want the whole month? Join Peter Xing live in Sydney on October 30.
